      "html": "<p>Corydoras loxozonus is among the most attractive members of the genus Corydoras and is also very easy to keep.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/corydoras_loxozonus_en/",
      "html": "<p>C. loxozonus originates from the Rio Orinoco and its affluents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/corydoras_loxozonus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species prefers higher temperatures. The water temperature should not sink below 25°C for longer periods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10a-catfishes-corydoras-co/corydoras_loxozonus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Among wild-collected fish, some specimens always appear with a rather broken dorsal band. Formerly these individuals were often mistaken for Corydoras evelynae. It is now known that Corydoras loxozonus can have a very variable pattern. Most experts believe that even such aberrant fish as C82 and C83 belong to this species.</p>"
    }
